-- title:
--   Eigenspace dimensions for a corner realisation at level N
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a characteristic-zero discrete valuation domain, complete for its maximal-ideal adic topology and with finite residue field $k=\mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal O$, and write $\bar K$ for `AlgebraicClosure (FractionRing 𝒪)`. Fix a finite set $S\subseteq\mathbb N$ and a level $N\neq 0$ all of whose prime divisors lie in $S$, and assume that the integral lattice [`CuspForm.intLattice N 2`](def/CuspForm_IntegralStructure.html#L3) spans the weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ over $\mathbb C$. Let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) (the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb C}$ of those cusp forms generated by the Hecke generators attached to $S$) to $k$, and let $T=$ [`CuspForm.heckeLocal N S 𝒪 θ`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131) be the associated localisation, with localisation map $\pi$. Let $M$ be an abelian group carrying compatible $\mathcal O$- and $T$-module structures. On $H^1=$ [`CohCarrier.H1 N ⊤ 𝒪`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L162), the $\mathcal O$-module of additive homomorphisms from $\Gamma_H(N)$ with $H=\top$ to $\mathcal O$, let `hcomm` assert that the operators [`CohCarrier.opFamily N ⊤ S 𝒪`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L91) indexed by the generators $T_\ell$ ($\ell$ prime, $\ell\notin S$, $\ell\nmid N$), $U_q$ ($q\mid N$ prime) and $\langle d\rangle$ commute pairwise, let $\bar\theta$ be any $k$-valued function on those generators, and let `Sp` be an idempotent splitting (complete orthogonal idempotents $e_i$, maximal ideals $\mathfrak m_i$ exhausting the maximal spectrum, with $e_i\in\mathfrak m_j$ iff $i\neq j$) of the $\mathcal O$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathcal O}(H^1)$ generated by these operators. Fix an index $i_0$ and an $\mathcal O$-linear isomorphism $e$ of $M$ with the corner $e_{i_0}H^1$, and assume that for every prime $\ell\notin S$ with $\ell\nmid N$ and every $m\in M$ the element $e(\pi(T_\ell)\cdot m)$ is, inside $H^1$, the image of $e(m)$ under the Hecke operator at $\ell$. Then for every $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphism $\chi\colon T\to\bar K$ the $\bar K$-dimension of the intersection over all $t\in T$ of the $\chi(t)$-eigenspaces of the base change to $\bar K$ of multiplication by $t$ on $M$ equals the $\bar K$-dimension of the intersection of the range of the base-changed inclusion $e_{i_0}H^1\hookrightarrow H^1$ with the intersection, over all primes $\ell\notin S$ with $\ell\nmid N$, of the $\chi(\pi(T_\ell))$-eigenspaces of the base change of [`CohCarrier.heckeTL N ⊤ 𝒪 ℓ`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L23).
--
--   This identifies the multiplicity of a $\bar K$-valued system of Hecke eigenvalues on an abstract module over the localised anemic Hecke algebra with the dimension of the corresponding common $T_\ell$-eigenspace inside the base-changed corner of $H^1(\Gamma_0(N),\mathcal O)$, the passage from the abstract to the cohomological side of a corner realisation at a single level. It is used in the newform-multiplicity statement for corner realisations at level $N$.
